# The generated string table is UTF-16LE with a BOM (Localization/build.ps1), and line-ending
# normalisation corrupts it: a newline is 0D 00 0A 00, whose 0A reads as a lone LF, and checkout
# rewrites it to 0D 00 0D 0A 00 -- one byte too many, and every code unit after it is misaligned.
#
# Git already infers this from the NUL bytes. Saying it means a later `* text=auto` cannot quietly
# undo it, since an explicit attribute wins over auto-detection.
src/DeskFlip/Localization/*.rc binary
